<template>
  <div class="touchless-panel q-pa-md" data-test="touchless-intelligence-panel">
    <div class="row items-center q-mb-md no-wrap">
      <TouchlessFilterBar
        :filters="store.filters"
        :doc-type-options="store.docTypeOptions"
        class="col"
        @change="onFiltersChange"
      />
      <!--
        The rate is only trustworthy if the reader can reconstruct it; the
        drawer shows the arithmetic against this org's own numbers.

        `icon` is a Material Icons LIGATURE name, not an "mdi:" one. A raw
        q-btn does not resolve the mdi prefix that TouchlessWidgetWrapper
        handles for its own icons — given "mdi:help-circle-outline" the
        Material Icons font rendered stray glyphs across this button's label.
      -->
      <!--
        Bulk analysis (DOCB-14285). The label carries the count BEFORE the
        click — "Analyse 5 clusters with AI" — because a button that starts a
        paid, minutes-long job must say how much of it it starts. The count is
        the backend's own selection (budget, minimum size, leverage order), not
        a tally of what happens to be on screen.

        Disabled at zero rather than hidden: a reader who expected the button
        should learn that nothing currently qualifies, not that the feature
        vanished.
      -->
      <!--
        The tooltip hangs on this wrapper, not inside the button (DOCB-14335).
        A disabled q-btn carries `pointer-events: none`, so a `<q-tooltip>`
        nested in it never opens — measured on dev: enabled renders a
        `.q-tooltip`, disabled renders nothing at all. Which meant the one
        state that has to explain itself was the one state that could not.
      -->
      <span
        v-if="bulkAdviceVisible"
        class="inline-flex"
        data-test="touchless-bulk-analyze-host"
      >
        <q-btn
          dense
          no-caps
          unelevated
          color="primary"
          icon="auto_awesome"
          class="q-ml-sm"
          :label="bulkAdviceLabel"
          :loading="bulkAdviceBusy"
          :disable="bulkAdviceDisabled"
          data-test="touchless-bulk-analyze"
          @click="onBulkAnalyze"
        />
        <q-tooltip v-if="bulkAdviceHint">{{ bulkAdviceHint }}</q-tooltip>
      </span>
      <!--
        And on screen as well as on hover (DOCB-14335): "the AI analysis is
        not configured in this environment" is not a detail to discover by
        hovering, it is the answer to why the button next to it can never be
        pressed here. Only ever a reason the backend actually named.
      -->
      <span
        v-if="bulkAdviceUnavailableReason"
        class="ml-2 text-xs text-muted-foreground"
        data-test="touchless-bulk-advisor-reason"
      >
        {{ bulkAdviceUnavailableReason }}
      </span>
      <!--
        Live progress for the run in flight (DOCB-14285). Beside the button
        rather than inside its label: the label is the button's PROMISE
        ("Analyse 5 clusters"), and overwriting it while the job runs would
        take away the one line that says what was started. Absent entirely when
        no run is being watched, so the toolbar does not carry a permanent
        "0/0".
      -->
      <!--
        Tailwind + semantic tokens, so it reads correctly in both themes with
        no dark-mode branch of its own. `tabular-nums` keeps "3/8" from
        shifting sideways as the digits change every few seconds.
      -->
      <span
        v-if="bulkProgressVisible"
        class="ml-2 whitespace-nowrap text-xs font-medium tabular-nums text-muted-foreground"
        data-test="touchless-bulk-progress"
      >
        {{ bulkProgressLabel }}
      </span>
      <!--
        What the click would actually do (DOCB-14312). The button used to read
        "Analyse 6 clusters with AI" for ever, so a second click looked exactly
        like the first even though the cache meant nothing was recomputed.
        These two lines are the difference, and they are on screen BEFORE the
        click rather than in a toast after it.

        Hidden while a run is being watched: the progress counter beside them
        is the live truth, and a stale "4 already analysed" next to a moving
        x/N reads as a contradiction.
      -->
      <span
        v-if="bulkBreakdownVisible"
        class="ml-2 whitespace-nowrap text-xs tabular-nums text-muted-foreground"
        data-test="touchless-bulk-breakdown"
      >
        {{ bulkBreakdownLabel }}
      </span>
      <!-- How much of the run is work the customer can act on (DOCB-14318).
           "6 clusters" reads as six opportunities; on dev three of the six
           could only ever be fixed by the supplier. -->
      <span
        v-if="bulkSplitVisible"
        class="ml-2 whitespace-nowrap text-xs tabular-nums text-muted-foreground"
        data-test="touchless-bulk-split"
      >
        {{ bulkSplitLabel }}
      </span>
      <span
        v-if="bulkLastAnalyzedVisible"
        class="ml-2 whitespace-nowrap text-xs text-muted-foreground"
        data-test="touchless-bulk-last-analyzed"
      >
        {{ bulkLastAnalyzedLabel }}
      </span>
      <q-btn
        flat
        dense
        no-caps
        icon="help_outline"
        :label="$t('touchless_how_calculated')"
        class="q-ml-sm"
        data-test="touchless-methodology-open"
        @click="methodologyOpen = true"
      />
    </div>

    <!--
      The scope the button does NOT narrow (DOCB-14313).

      A sub-organisation in the header filters everything else on this page,
      and deliberately does not filter this button (DOCB-14288) — so the
      honest reading of the screen is the wrong one unless the difference is
